WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.897 --> 00:00:06.730
- Good morning, folks.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.440
I just decided that I want to do another

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.200
What I Eat in a Day video.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.290
I thought about the
one I did two years ago

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.850
and a lot has changed,
not only in my routine,

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.340
but also in my YouTube videos.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.980
That one was just so cringe-y.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.280
...energy to be utilized
throughout the day...

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.810
Ah, so I'm going to take you through

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.770
what I eat for breakfast, lunch, dinner,

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:25.773
and everything in between,

00:00:25.773 --> 00:00:28.340
with the help of my partner, Lifesum,

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.590
who is going to help me track my calories,

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.300
macro nutrients, micro
nutrients, all that good stuff.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.670
Are you ready to come along for the ride?

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.530
Gimme five, oh you
missed it, one more time.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.870
No this hand, this one, gimme five, yeah!

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.260
My breakfast has changed a
little bit since my last video.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.730
So let me show you what I
eat for breakfast nowadays.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:48.730
This is my breakfast.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.630
Lately, I haven't been eating breakfast.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.950
I've become a huge fan
of intermittent fasting

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.810
where I have 14 to 16
hours since my last meal.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:58.060
Like right now I'm about to
go on national television.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.203
I have to be super sharp, talk about CBD,

00:01:00.203 --> 00:01:01.450
kind of interesting.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:02.930
If you guys want to hear more about CBD,

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.150
drop it down below in the comments.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:06.340
I'm going to go on TV
without eating anything.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:08.780
I feel sharper; I feel more engaged.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.380
This is consistent with
some of the leading research

00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:14.420
that's showing intermittent
fasting can be a good idea.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:15.367
Now it's not right for everybody,

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:16.750
and I don't recommend you start it without

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.060
chatting with a doctor first,

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.200
but it certainly works for me.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.400
I need a little caffeine kick

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.080
but I'm not a huge fan of overdoing it.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.747
I drink my magic sauce,
and that's green tea.

00:01:29.686 --> 00:01:33.437
- [Astronaut Voice]
Ignition sequence start:

00:01:33.437 --> 00:01:38.437
six, five, four, three, two, one, zero.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:41.303
All engines running.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.220
- Now my fresh cup of tea is ready to go.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:47.427
As I told you in my hot tea video,

00:01:47.427 --> 00:01:48.930
you don't want to drink anything

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.230
that's above 140 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:53.000
So I do let it chill for a little bit

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.080
before I take a sip.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.620
It gives me a nice little boost
with a tiny bit of caffeine

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.230
instead of that caffeine kick that I get

00:01:58.230 --> 00:01:59.570
if I'm drinking a cup of coffee.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:01.600
I need that sometimes,
but not most mornings.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.830
Especially when I'm going on television,

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:03.788
I don't want to look crazy.

00:02:03.788 --> 00:02:07.705
(voice playback at high speed)

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:17.320
All right I got this yummy bowl of steak,

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.100
sweet potatoes, broccoli.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:22.120
Over here I got my avocado
toast with some sriracha flakes.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.940
This bowl is a go-to bowl for me.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.560
It has protein; It has
complex carbohydrates,

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.126
anti-oxidants from the broccoli.

00:02:28.126 --> 00:02:30.325
And on top of it, it has romesco sauce:

00:02:30.325 --> 00:02:32.350
olive oil, healthy fats.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.630
You know they say you are what you eat.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.243
I guess I must be nutritious.

00:02:36.243 --> 00:02:38.520
I'm going to pull up my Lifesum app here

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.930
and enter what I ate.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:43.640
Muti-grain...if I can spell...toast,

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:48.010
guacamole, single
potato, steak: grass fed.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:51.750
So for lunch I've
already had 773 calories,

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.630
which is really close to my 800 goal.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.960
The only thing is, my
sodium is quite high.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.040
That's because I'm eating out.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.380
There's a lot of sauces, there's
a lot of sodium in there.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.660
I'm going to cut myself
a break on this one meal

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.480
and go 200mg over.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.080
So you may have noticed, Bear is wearing

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.780
his in-training jacket.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.130
The biggest reason he needs that jacket,

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.090
is just so inconsiderate dog owners

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.350
don't let their dogs just run up to him,

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.430
because some people think that all dogs

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:16.859
should just be playing
while they're on leash.

00:03:16.859 --> 00:03:18.570
That is not the case.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.710
Dogs need to respect other dogs' space

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:23.300
and that's part of teaching
your dog proper etiquette.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.440
That's how you train a pup.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:25.800
Now a lot of you may not know this,

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.500
but I'm pretty good at basketball.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.047
Making it rain...Dr. J!

00:03:48.143 --> 00:03:50.520
I've told you before that I like doing

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.250
all different types of
activities to stay fit.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.250
Basketball is one of them.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.020
If I can't find game, I'm
just going to go ahead

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.640
and just dribble by myself.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:00.020
You know, I could play
one-on-one-on-one-on-one,

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.963
which is with my imaginary self.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.995
Banks open on Tuesdays, folks.

00:04:05.995 --> 00:04:08.140
All right, I'm about to grab my favorite

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.170
post-workout snack, it may surprise you.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:12.350
Not a huge fan of post-workout shakes

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.570
because they make me feel bloated.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:15.780
So I get some berries and mango.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.370
This is like really good fiber, sugars,

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.606
to get that insulin
kick after your workout.

00:04:21.606 --> 00:04:26.100
And then the magic
sauce, boiled whole eggs.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.290
A lot of people don't like these,

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:28.900
'cause they think they're tasteless.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:29.980
I think they're delicious.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.950
Then, because I need some
electrolytes to refuel,

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:35.080
I'm gonna get some pink
Himalayan salt here.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.936
Dip, get a little bit of
salt on there, just a pinch.

00:04:37.936 --> 00:04:41.187
A lot of people say, oh I don't like it

00:04:41.187 --> 00:04:43.340
without ketchup and mayo.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.954
Look, if you need a dab of
ketchup or a dab of mayo

00:04:45.954 --> 00:04:48.960
to make a healthy meal
appetizing, make it happen.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.960
Just don't throw in a whole
three tablespoons of mayo

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.820
and expect that meal to still be healthy.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.310
Now, I go into my favorite part.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:01.270
Blueberries, one of the
most antioxidant rich

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.780
berries out there, one of
the best fruits to eat.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.000
Hard boiled egg,
blueberries, strawberries,

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.800
and then last but not least mango.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:14.800
Here's our stats: 334
calories, 17 grams of protein,

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:20.960
31 grams of carbs, 16 grams
of fat, 160mg of sodium.

00:05:21.504 --> 00:05:24.010
Now the sodium might
be a little bit higher

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.780
'cause I did sprinkle a
little bit on my eggs,

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.790
but I think that's pretty
negligible at this point.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:29.500
Now it's time for me take a shower,

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:32.130
kick back, relax a little bit with Bear,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:35.081
maybe a little Netflix and
chill if you know what I mean.

00:05:35.081 --> 00:05:37.700
Who Netflix's and chills with their dog?

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:38.893
He loves to wrestle.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.250
Look at him, he just collapses.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.870
I'm going to enjoy myself a Greek salad

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.140
with grilled chicken.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:04.990
Greek salad is the way to go.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.400
You're getting tomatoes,
cucumbers, olives,

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.640
all power vegetables.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.160
You got your grilled chicken,
clean source of protein.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.520
A little olive oil and vinegar,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.430
just for the extra little taste kick.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:17.608
After a long day, filming,
hanging out with Bear,

00:06:17.608 --> 00:06:21.560
doing TV, this is a nice
thing to come home to.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.070
And I'm gonna say, this is
roughly 8 ounces of chicken,

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:27.830
a small avocado, half a
tomato, 1 ounce of olive oil.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.700
There was a little feta
in here, feta, feta.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.720
We got 829 calories in this meal.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:35.968
71 grams of protein, 22
carbs, 54 grams of fat,

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:40.180
all healthy fat, sodium
1216 which is under

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.500
what I'm supposed to be
eating for this meal.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.980
And this is a perfect dinner for me,

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:43.950
at least for my goals.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.210
Look at that feta, yum.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.500
For those of you who have
not lived in Manhattan,

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.760
storage comes at a premium.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.770
So when I get a lot of groceries,

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:54.824
I have to store them in, of all places,

00:06:54.824 --> 00:06:57.220
in my dishwasher.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.640
And I know that's really funny to say,

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:02.620
but I don't use the dishwasher a lot.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:05.250
I order out a lot and
if I'm washing dishes

00:07:06.475 --> 00:07:07.830
I can just do 'em by
hand in the dishwash...

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.590
In the dishwasher? No, in the sink.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:12.903
What I do use it for
is for storing my nuts.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:18.170
I love nuts; I'm actually not
joking I really do love nuts.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.300
That's about half a cup.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.400
I feel like you guys are going to be

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.963
judging me so hard for
using my dishwasher.

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:26.060
Look, my dishwasher is confused already.

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.310
It turned on because
it's like, is it time?

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:29.720
No, it's not time.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.070
There's groceries inside
here, don't wash them.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.670
Healthy fats galore here.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:37.040
Even a little bit of protein
to finish off my day.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.870
What I want you do understand
from watching me today,

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:41.500
having my final snack here,

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:42.820
this is what I ate today.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.600
It's not what I eat everyday.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.370
That's an important distinction.

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:48.643
And one of the most
important distinctions,

00:07:48.643 --> 00:07:51.620
is that this diet that I follow,

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:53.620
this specific eating plan that I follow,

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.120
is not for everybody.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.740
Now it's what works for me;
it's what I'm eating right now.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.833
That may change, but again nutrition

00:07:59.833 --> 00:08:01.710
has to be individualized.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.525
It's different for person A, for person B,

00:08:03.525 --> 00:08:04.920
and even person C.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.000
I bet you didn't expect I was
throwing person C in there.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.500
Bear likes hanging out with me

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:13.230
while I eat nuts, because
obviously bears love nuts.

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.640
I actually don't know if that's a thing.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.783
I'm 49 calories over, which means that

00:08:16.783 --> 00:08:19.540
I'm right in the right spot for calories.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.470
I under ate my protein just a little bit,

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:22.760
but I over ate fats.

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.800
That's going to happen
on a day to day variance.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.717
Remember, this is what
I eat in a day today,

00:08:26.717 --> 00:08:28.310
not what I eat everyday.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:29.690
There's going to be some variation.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.290
A really simple take away for you:

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:34.480
decrease the refined sugars,
decrease the processed foods,

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.370
and increase the fruits and vegetables

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.757
and plants in your diet,
as well as those proteins,

00:08:38.757 --> 00:08:40.850
'cause that's how you
stay happy and healthy.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.650
And speaking of happy and healthy,

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:45.470
as always, Bear do you want to do it?

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:49.180
As always, stay happy and
healthy, coming from Bear.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.430
And check out this video.

